## Metadata
Title: FUN'S Cross-Word Puzzle
Copyright: New York World
Date: 1914-05-31
Number: 22
Description: An hourglass 19 wide and 11 high (19 squares in the top and bottom rows, narrowing by one square each side to 9 in the middle row, squares outside shown as _), with shaded squares inside the outline making two X shapes; they are printed shaded, not black, and stand as blocks (#).
Source: Milwaukee Sentinel, 1914-05-31, p. 90
Solution-Source: Milwaukee Sentinel, 1914-06-07, p. 85


## Printed
heading: FUN'S CROSS-WORD PUZZLE
number: No 22
intro: Here is number twenty-one in FUN'S series of cross word puzzles. It is different from any of the others published thus far and you will find yourself busily engaged for some time to come when you begin to solve it. Fill in the small squares in the above diamond with words corresponding to the clews and definitions given herewith. The solution will appear in next week's FUN.
solution heading: SOLUTION TO LAST WEEK'S PUZZLE.
solution caption: Herewith is given the solution to cross-word puzzle No. 22, given in last week's Fun. The diagram shows how the letters should be arranged to fit the list of clews and definitions given.


